 # Work summary and next action
 
+## Current outcome — 2026-10-28
+
+Both controlled arms completed400 updates. Retain camera2200: no screened
+endpoint was nominal-eligible. Control +400 scored45/256 nominal and29/256
+wide; data-first +400 scored4/256 nominal and11/256 wide, versus baseline
+229/256 and80/256. The +200 endpoints also failed the nominal gate.
+All screens passed paired provenance/pose validation. No eligible candidate
+remained for1024-start confirmation; it was not run. No extension is queued.
+Initial diagnosis locates the collapse mainly between grasp and lift. Data-first
+replaced every older replay row and more than doubled error on fixed earlier
+examples, while fitting newer replay. Normalizer drift is small and swapping
+baseline statistics barely changes offline errors. These findings support
+forgetting but do not establish the full task-level cause. Next diagnostic:
+compare per-joint errors on fixed reference grasp-to-lift trajectories before
+further training. [Diagnosis](../logs/camera_controlled_20261028_111754/DIAGNOSIS.md).
+Full evidence: [experiment report](../logs/camera_controlled_20261028_111754/REPORT.md).
